<title>UK: DB Capital Markets sets warrants on dollar/mark.</title>
<headline>DB Capital Markets sets warrants on dollar/mark.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>DB Capital Markets has issued three million European-style call with cap warrants, in three equal tranches, on the U.S. dollar/mark, lead manager Deutsche Bank said.</p>
<p>COMMON TERMS:</p>
<p> EXPIRATION	15.DEC.97		 PAYDATE	10.DEC.96</p>
<p> LISTING	   FFURT, DUSS	     MIN SUB	100</p>
<p> SPOT REFERENCE  US$/DEM 1.5615 DEM</p>
<p> *  *  *  *  *  *</p>
<p> TYPE		STRIKE	CAP	  ISSUE</p>
<p> CALL WITH CAP   1.45 DEM    1.50 DEM   5.81 DEM</p>
<p> CALL WITH CAP   1.50 DEM    1.60 DEM   4.30 DEM</p>
<p> CALL WITH CAP   1.55 DEM    1.65 DEM   2.97 DEM</p>
<p> NOTES    MAXIMUM PAYOUT IS 10.0 DEM PER WARRANT.</p>
<p>--Reuter London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
